.* Blackjack help - English
:userdoc.

:h1 res=001.General Help
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Blackjack is the casino card game also known as Twenty-One. You play against the dealer and try to get closer to 21 than the dealer without going over. Choose a topic&colon.
:p.
:ul compact.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=002.Playing:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=003.Game rules:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=004.Menus:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=005.About Blackjack and license:elink.
:eul.
:p.

:h1 res=002.Playing
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
You start with $100 in the bank. Set your wager (from $5 to $100) in the field at the left and press :hp2.Deal:ehp2.. You and the dealer each get two cards; one dealer card stays face down.
:p.
Card values&colon. cards 2 to 10 count their number, Jack, Queen and King count 10, an Ace counts 1 or 11. Your hand value is shown below your cards.
:dl tsize=14.
:dt.:hp2.Hit:ehp2.
:dd.Take another card. If you go over 21 you bust and lose your wager.
:dt.:hp2.Stand:ehp2.
:dd.Keep your hand. The dealer then plays.
:dt.:hp2.Double:ehp2.
:dd.Doubles your wager, you receive exactly one more card and your hand ends.
:dt.:hp2.Split:ehp2.
:dd.If your first two cards have the same value you may split them into two hands with a second wager. You can split up to four hands.
:edl.
:p.
If the dealer shows an Ace you are offered :hp2.insurance:ehp2. for half your wager. A Blackjack (an Ace and a ten-value card) pays 3 to 2 unless the dealer also has Blackjack, then it is a push. A win pays even money, a push returns your wager.
:p.
The bar on the right shows the shoe. When the red marker is reached the cards are shuffled before the next hand. If the bank cannot cover a wager, use :hp2.Game - Add $100:ehp2..

:h1 res=003.Game rules
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Choose :hp2.Options - Rules:ehp2. to change&colon.
:ul compact.
:li.Player can resplit aces&colon. split hands made from aces may be split again.
:li.Dealer hits soft 17&colon. the dealer takes a card on a soft 17 (an Ace counted as 11). When off, the dealer stands on all 17.
:li.Double 10/11 only&colon. doubling is allowed only on a hand value of 10 or 11.
:li.Number of decks&colon. 2 to 8 decks in the shoe. A new value applies at the next shuffle.
:eul.

:h1 res=004.Menus
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
:dl tsize=18.
:dt.:hp2.New Game:ehp2. (Ctrl+N)
:dd.Clears the table and sets the bank back to $100. Only between hands.
:dt.:hp2.Add $100:ehp2.
:dd.Adds $100 to the bank.
:dt.:hp2.Cash Out:ehp2.
:dd.Shows how much you take home and empties the bank. Only between hands.
:dt.:hp2.Exit:ehp2. (Ctrl+X)
:dd.Leaves the game.
:dt.:hp2.Options - Sound:ehp2.
:dd.Switches the sound effects on or off.
:dt.:hp2.Options - Language:ehp2.
:dd.English, Spanish, Dutch, German, French or Italian. Menus, dialogs and this help change at once.
:dt.:hp2.Frame Controls:ehp2. (Ctrl+F)
:dd.Hides or shows the title bar and the menu.
:dt.:hp2.Save settings on exit:ehp2.
:dd.Saves the settings, the bank and the wager in BJack.cfg when you exit.
:edl.

:h1 res=005.About Blackjack and license
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Blackjack is part of The Compulsive Gambler's Toolkit by IglooSoft (1999), released as open source in 2002. The Open Watcom version was prepared by the OS2World community in 2026.
:p.
Blackjack is free software&colon. you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or (at your option) any later version. It is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY. See the file LICENSE.txt.

:euserdoc.
